              "en": "Beyond APOE, mutations within other genetic risk factors for AD, such as rare presenilin-1 (PSEN1) mutations are associated with early-onset AD, cause lysosomal mislocalization of the gamma-secretase complex, resulting in an intracellular pool of aggregation-prone Abeta42.While PSEN1 is known to directly regulate lysosomal acidification and function, the effect of apoE4 on lysosomal homeostasis remains incompletely explored.",
