        "boundary_en": "Credit a supported comparison of both intervention directions, linked to representative outcomes and correctly identified models; the examples and signaling nodes above are not an exhaustive checklist. Human expression observations can supply context but cannot establish intervention causality. Do not assume that more PINK1 is universally beneficial: cytosolic sPINK1-driven ubiquitin phosphorylation can impair proteasomal function in other experimental settings. However, the knockout-associated reduction of aggregation in G4-D was tested in aging/MCAO-ischemia mice and MG132-treated HEK293 cells, not in an AD-mouse knockout experiment. A properly bounded discussion is acceptable; calling this proof that PINK1 knockout protects against AD is not. Database hypothesis labels and repeated reviews of one experiment do not independently establish mechanisms. [G4-D](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12313235/)",
