        {
          "en": "**Direct answer:** The tau hypothesis centers on pathological tau species—hyperphosphorylated, misfolded, oligomeric, and fibrillar tau forming neuropil threads, neurofibrillary tangles (NFTs), and dystrophic neurites—as drivers of AD neurodegeneration. It also implicates tau propagation, synaptic/axonal dysfunction, and tau–amyloid interaction, but the strongest human evidence links tau burden to cognitive decline rather than proving tau is the primary cause.",
          "zh": "**直接回答：** tau假说聚焦于病理性tau种类——过度磷酸化、错误折叠、寡聚化和纤维状tau形成神经毡线、神经原纤维缠结（NFTs）和营养不良性神经突——作为AD神经退行性变的驱动因素。它还涉及tau传播、突触/轴突功能障碍以及tau–淀粉样蛋白相互作用，但最强的人类证据将tau负荷与认知下降联系起来，而非证明tau是主要原因。"
        },
        {
          "en": "**Key phenotypes and evidence**",
          "zh": "**关键表型和证据**"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Hyperphosphorylated and abnormally folded tau:** Phospho-tau (e.g., AT8, PHF-1, MC1) accumulates in neuronal processes and somata. This is a defining AD phenotype and correlates with Braak stage (Braak & Braak, 1991, PMID: 1992935).",
          "zh": "- **过度磷酸化和异常折叠的tau：** 磷酸化tau（例如AT8、PHF-1、MC1）在神经元突起和胞体中积累。这是AD的一个定义性表型，并与Braak分期相关（Braak & Braak, 1991, PMID: 1992935）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Neurofibrillary tangles (NFTs):** Paired helical filaments of tau form NFTs in entorhinal cortex, hippocampus, and neocortex. NFT topography defines Braak staging and correlates with dementia severity better than amyloid plaque density in many clinicopathological studies (Braak & Braak, 1991, PMID: 1992935; Arriagada et al., 1992, PMID: 1566067).",
          "zh": "- **神经原纤维缠结（NFTs）：** tau的双螺旋丝形成NFTs，位于内嗅皮层、海马和新皮层。NFT地形学定义了Braak分期，并且在许多临床病理学研究中与痴呆严重程度的相关性优于淀粉样斑块密度（Braak & Braak, 1991, PMID: 1992935; Arriagada et al., 1992, PMID: 1566067）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Neuropil threads and dystrophic neurites:** These tau-positive structures surround plaques and contribute to synaptic loss, a strong correlate of cognitive impairment (Masliah et al., 1991, PMID: 1891093).",
          "zh": "- **神经毡线和营养不良性神经突：** 这些tau阳性结构围绕斑块，并导致突触丢失，后者是认知障碍的强相关因素（Masliah et al., 1991, PMID: 1891093）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Tau oligomers and soluble tau:** Soluble oligomeric tau is implicated in synaptic toxicity and memory deficits in animal models; human postmortem studies associate soluble tau with cognitive decline, but causation in humans remains inferential (Walsh & Selkoe, 2004, PMID: 15217324; Berger et al., 2007, PMID: 17360906).",
          "zh": "- **tau寡聚体和可溶性tau：** 可溶性寡聚tau在动物模型中涉及突触毒性和记忆缺陷；人类尸检研究将可溶性tau与认知下降联系起来，但在人类中的因果关系仍是推断性的（Walsh & Selkoe, 2004, PMID: 15217324; Berger et al., 2007, PMID: 17360906）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Tau propagation:** Cell-to-cell spread of misfolded tau is supported by animal and cellular models and by human graft studies, but the extent to which this drives AD progression in humans is not fully established (Clavaguera et al., 2009, PMID: 19242475; Braak & Del Tredici, 2011, PMID: 21292315).",
          "zh": "- **tau传播：** 错误折叠tau的细胞间扩散得到动物和细胞模型以及人类移植研究的支持，但这在多大程度上驱动人类AD进展尚未完全确立（Clavaguera et al., 2009, PMID: 19242475; Braak & Del Tredici, 2011, PMID: 21292315）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "- **Tau–amyloid interaction:** Amyloid-beta may promote tau pathology; human imaging shows tau PET uptake correlates with cognition and amyloid status, but the causal direction remains debated (Jack et al., 2013, PMID: 23623694; Busche & Hyman, 2020, PMID: 32698675).",
          "zh": "- **tau–淀粉样蛋白相互作用：** 淀粉样蛋白-beta可能促进tau病理；人类影像显示tau PET摄取与认知和淀粉样蛋白状态相关，但因果方向仍有争议（Jack et al., 2013, PMID: 23623694; Busche & Hyman, 2020, PMID: 32698675）。"
        },
        {
          "en": "**Limitations and uncertainty**",
          "zh": "**局限性和不确定性**"
        },
        {
          "en": "NFTs are a robust association with dementia, but whether tau is the primary driver or a downstream mediator of amyloid toxicity is unresolved. Most mechanistic evidence for tau oligomers and propagation comes from cell and animal models; human causal evidence is limited. Anti-tau therapies have not yet shown clear disease-modifying benefit, so the tau hypothesis remains strong but not proven as the sole cause.",
          "zh": "NFTs与痴呆有稳健的关联，但tau是主要驱动因素还是淀粉样蛋白毒性的下游介质尚未解决。大多数关于tau寡聚体和传播的机制证据来自细胞和动物模型；人类因果证据有限。抗tau疗法尚未显示出明确的疾病修饰益处，因此tau假说仍然有力，但未被证明是唯一原因。"
        }
