      "original_en": "**Direct answer:** The neuroinflammation hypothesis of AD is linked to several immune signaling pathways, most consistently microglial TREM2–TYROBP signaling, the CD33/SPI1–PU.1 axis, complement (C1q/C3), cytokine–JAK/STAT and NF-κB signaling, and chemokine/cytokine networks (IL-34, CX3CR1, TNF/TNFR2, IL-1β, IFN-γ).\n\n**Supporting points**\n- **TREM2–TYROBP:** TREM2 is a central microglial regulator; loss-of-function variants (e.g., R47H) impair phagocytosis and immune homeostasis and raise late-onset AD risk (PMID 41580393; 41512220). The T96K variant weakened microglial activation in female mice in vivo, showing model-dependent effects (PMID 41570801). CD33 and SPI1 variants converge to reduce phagocytosis and surface TREM2 (PMID 41279508).\n- **PU.1/IRF8–TGFβ1:** PU.1 and IRF8 directly target the TGFβ1 locus, controlling microglial TGFβ1 induction during neurodegeneration (PMID 41634038). PU.1 binding also mediates PICALM LOAD-risk effects on Aβ/myelin uptake (PMID 40903578).\n- **Complement:** Microglial C1q deletion reduced synapse engulfment and preserved cognition in AD mice without changing amyloid burden, implicating complement in synaptic, not plaque, pathology (PMID 41000995).\n- **Cytokine signaling:** PSEN1-mutant astrocytes show reduced IFNAR2 surface expression, lower STAT2 phosphorylation, and delayed NF-κB nuclear localization after inflammatory stimuli (PMID 40542358). ABCA7-A696S disturbed IL-1β and IFN-γ induction in 5xFAD mice (PMID 39880319). TNFR2 blockade improved synaptic potentiation in 5xFAD synaptosomes (PMID 40527437).\n- **Chemokine/other immune nodes:** IL-34 deletion depleted homeostatic microglia and impaired plaque encapsulation in APP/PS1 mice (PMID 42396292); CX3CR1-V249I altered human microglial Aβ uptake and migration (PMID 40631275).\n\n**Limitations**\nMost evidence is from mouse or cell models (e.g., 5xFAD, APP/PS1, iPSC-microglia), so associations do not establish causation in humans. Findings conflict by variant, sex, and model (e.g., TREM2 T96K; PMID 41570801). One cited record is retracted (PMID 41384297) and is not relied upon here. Human causal evidence for specific pathways remains limited.",
      "original_zh": "**直接回答：** AD的神经炎症假说与多条免疫信号通路相关，其中最一致的是小胶质细胞TREM2–TYROBP信号、CD33/SPI1–PU.1轴、补体（C1q/C3）、细胞因子–JAK/STAT和NF-κB信号，以及趋化因子/细胞因子网络（IL-34、CX3CR1、TNF/TNFR2、IL-1β、IFN-γ）。\n\n**支持要点**\n\n- **TREM2–TYROBP：** TREM2是小胶质细胞的核心调节因子；功能丧失变异（如R47H）损害吞噬作用和免疫稳态，并提高迟发性AD风险（PMID 41580393；41512220）。T96K变异在雌性小鼠体内减弱了小胶质细胞激活，显示出模型依赖性效应（PMID 41570801）。CD33和SPI1变异汇聚于降低吞噬作用和表面TREM2（PMID 41279508）。\n\n- **PU.1/IRF8–TGFβ1：** PU.1和IRF8直接靶向TGFβ1位点，在神经退行过程中控制小胶质细胞TGFβ1的诱导（PMID 41634038）。PU.1结合还介导PICALM LOAD风险对Aβ/髓鞘摄取的影响（PMID 40903578）。\n\n- **补体：** 在AD小鼠中，小胶质细胞C1q缺失减少了突触吞噬并保留了认知，而未改变淀粉样蛋白负荷，提示补体参与突触而非斑块病理（PMID 41000995）。\n\n- **细胞因子信号：** PSEN1突变星形胶质细胞在炎症刺激后显示IFNAR2表面表达降低、STAT2磷酸化降低以及NF-κB核定位延迟（PMID 40542358）。ABCA7-A696S扰乱了5xFAD小鼠中IL-1β和IFN-γ的诱导（PMID 39880319）。TNFR2阻断改善了5xFAD突触体中的突触增强（PMID 40527437）。\n\n- **趋化因子/其他免疫节点：** IL-34缺失耗竭了稳态小胶质细胞并损害了APP/PS1小鼠中的斑块包裹（PMID 42396292）；CX3CR1-V249I改变了人类小胶质细胞Aβ摄取和迁移（PMID 40631275）。\n\n**局限性**\n大多数证据来自小鼠或细胞模型（如5xFAD、APP/PS1、iPSC-小胶质细胞），因此关联不能确立人类中的因果关系。研究结果因变异、性别和模型而相互冲突（如TREM2 T96K；PMID 41570801）。一条被引用的记录已被撤稿（PMID 41384297），此处未依赖该记录。特定通路的人类因果证据仍然有限。\n"
