          "en": "**Direct answer:** The oxidative stress hypothesis and mitochondrial dysfunction in AD are linked by molecular evidence showing that amyloid-β (Aβ) and hyperphosphorylated tau impair mitochondrial electron transport, increase reactive oxygen species (ROS), and damage mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA), while oxidative damage in turn amplifies Aβ production and tau pathology. This creates a feed-forward cycle, but most mechanistic evidence comes from cell and animal models; human data are largely correlative.",
          "zh": "**直接回答：** AD中的氧化应激假说与线粒体功能障碍通过分子证据相联系，这些证据表明淀粉样蛋白-β（Aβ）和过度磷酸化的tau损害线粒体电子传递、增加活性氧（ROS）并损伤线粒体DNA（mtDNA），而氧化损伤反过来又放大Aβ产生和tau病理。这形成了一个前馈循环，但大多数机制证据来自细胞和动物模型；人类数据在很大程度上是相关性的。"
